@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+---
+'@cashu/coco-core': minor
+---
+
+Add `offline` to `ops.send.prepare` and `Manager.setOffline`. An offline send is prepared from the
+mint's stored keysets without contacting it, and succeeds only when held proofs exactly match the
+amount (found by an exact subset search, not the randomized selector); otherwise it fails before
+reserving anything. A failed refresh of
+stale mint data now falls back to the stored data instead of throwing, and no refresh is attempted
+while offline; a swap send checks the mint is reachable before reserving anything. Executing an exact-match send no longer refreshes mint data.
